      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cytofluorometric determination of DNA content was done on paraffin-embedded tissues of 19 cases of coronary arteriosclerotic lesions including fibrocellular intimal thickening lesions (FT) or atherosclerosis (AS). DNA distribution pattern of medial smooth muscle cells of coronary arteries with FT and AS was all diploid. The average proliferative index (PI) of both medial smooth muscle cells of coronary arteries with FT and AS was 4.8 +/- 0.6. DNA distribution patterns of intimal cells of coronary arteries with FT and AS were also diploid. The average PI of intimal cells of coronary arteries with FT and AS was 8.4 +/- 1.0 and 9.1 +/- 0.7, respectively. These results suggest that intimal cellular proliferation plays an important role in the development of atherosclerosis."},
